Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:18:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] fix(gateway): rate limit by authenticated tenant, not
 request headers

The limiter keyed buckets on the X-Tenant-ID header before the
authenticated context, and its anonymous fallback trusted the first
X-Forwarded-For entry. Either way a client could get a fresh token bucket
per request by rotating a header value.

Key buckets on the tenant that Authenticate stored in the request
context, and fall back to the TCP peer address only when no tenant is
present. RateLimit no longer needs the tenant header name.
